{"data": [{"author_id": "1644034310993788928", "conversation_id": "2117375878900621755", "created_at": "2026-11-03T01:03:50.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117422464967880993"], "id": "2117422464967880993", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus If models can read and edit weights directly, evals get harder too. Who checks the edit didn't quietly break something the benchmark doesn't measure?", "url": "https://x.com/froggernauter/status/2117422464967880993"}, {"author_id": "1358053503088918528", "conversation_id": "2117375878900621755", "created_at": "2026-11-03T00:59:57.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117421490971066660"], "id": "2117421490971066660", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus imagine multiple instances of astra improving one astra model its huge", "url": "https://x.com/RaelBrucewayne/status/2117421490971066660"}, {"author_id": "1720665183188922368", "conversation_id": "2117375878900621755", "created_at": "2026-11-03T00:53:04.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117419756751872269"], "id": "2117419756751872269", "lang": "ru", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@Markins7dku @kimmonismus Это исследование MIT CSAIL (Takehi и др.) от 2 ноября 2026 — Weight-Space Programming. GPT-6 Astra напрямую читает и правит веса нейросетей без градиентов и обучения: изменил всего 0,016% весов Qwen3.5-0.8B и поднял MATH-500 с 7,9% до 48,1%. Claude аналогично пишет рабочие веса с", "url": "https://x.com/grok/status/2117419756751872269"}, {"author_id": "2102187446196719616", "conversation_id": "2117375878900621755", "created_at": "2026-11-03T00:52:35.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117419635729686860"], "id": "2117419635729686860", "lang": "ru", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus @grok что за релиз?", "url": "https://x.com/Markins7dku/status/2117419635729686860"}, {"author_id": "1331495798488653824", "conversation_id": "2117375878900621755", "created_at": "2026-11-03T00:34:46.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117415150789574676"], "id": "2117415150789574676", "lang": "qme", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 9, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus @kimmonismus https://t.co/nuti93DZLY", "url": "https://x.com/NockyLucky/status/2117415150789574676"}, {"author_id": "102867203", "conversation_id": "2117375878900621755", "created_at": "2026-11-03T00:24:31.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117412572638880013"], "id": "2117412572638880013", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus Agree on the direction. Once models start improving models, the scarce thing stops being ideas and becomes verification. Whoever has the best evals runs the safest loop.", "url": "https://x.com/RuedanaYT/status/2117412572638880013"}, {"author_id": "2110550226989711360", "conversation_id": "2117375878900621755", "created_at": "2026-11-03T00:24:07.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117412472575381915"], "id": "2117412472575381915", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus maybe. so far it's a 0.8B model and mostly math though, I'd want to see it hold up on a big model before calling it a giant step", "url": "https://x.com/plainAItips/status/2117412472575381915"}, {"author_id": "2116579414813065216", "conversation_id": "2117375878900621755", "created_at": "2026-11-03T00:15:31.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117410308616835088"], "id": "2117410308616835088", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus the Gemma section is the part I'd want in the RSI argument. on a model that didn't loop, Astra couldn't move MATH-500 more than about a point, and the authors flag that themselves", "url": "https://x.com/ContextWindowed/status/2117410308616835088"}, {"author_id": "2116797194372034560", "conversation_id": "2117375878900621755", "created_at": "2026-11-03T00:15:30.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117410304833306875"], "id": "2117410304833306875", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus The missing control is a baseline: edit the same 0.016% of weights at random, or do a tiny fine-tune, and compare on held-out math. Fixing reasoning loops in a 0.8B model could be a narrow patch rather than general improvement, and it says little about recursion.", "url": "https://x.com/leochenlab/status/2117410304833306875"}, {"author_id": "2086370229396111360", "conversation_id": "2117375878900621755", "created_at": "2026-11-03T00:05:18.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117407737248153998"], "id": "2117407737248153998", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus Editing a 0.8B model's weights is still a long way from a model improving itself. The real test: does the trick work on a model close to the editor's own size, and do the gains hold on held-out evals without breaking other skills?", "url": "https://x.com/miaojiang88/status/2117407737248153998"}, {"author_id": "2007976461031096320", "conversation_id": "2117375878900621755", "created_at": "2026-11-02T23:44:38.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117402534969245918"], "id": "2117402534969245918", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus Worth reading next to Haseeb Qureshi's clarification: Astra found a published interpretability technique and implemented it, and most of the 7.9% to 48.1% jump came from fixing a looping failure so the model actually finishes problems. Both can be true: the approach is promising,", "url": "https://x.com/zhuhaotian512/status/2117402534969245918"}, {"author_id": "2094540909996048384", "conversation_id": "2117375878900621755", "created_at": "2026-11-02T23:37:29.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117400735017025595"], "id": "2117400735017025595", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 24, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus It gets harder and harder each day to dismiss we’re in a simulation", "url": "https://x.com/EthanSDE/status/2117400735017025595"}, {"author_id": "417508671", "conversation_id": "2117375878900621755", "created_at": "2026-11-02T23:26:56.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117398082363015659"], "id": "2117398082363015659", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 13, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus Direct weight editing is exciting; it could become part of that loop. The recursive leap is showing that the improved system gets better at producing the next improvement, which the reported math gains alone don’t establish.", "url": "https://x.com/thesimaximalist/status/2117398082363015659"}, {"author_id": "2076808453176299520", "conversation_id": "2117375878900621755", "created_at": "2026-11-02T23:14:19.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117394907472224711"], "id": "2117394907472224711", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 39, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus I imagine all the labs are doing this by pointing their new models at older models…. I know the prompt they use: “make it better” 😅", "url": "https://x.com/MJmd26/status/2117394907472224711"}, {"author_id": "1543134949808558080", "conversation_id": "2117375878900621755", "created_at": "2026-11-02T23:09:24.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117393668097310944"], "id": "2117393668097310944", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus It does present an interesting theory though", "url": "https://x.com/JngPing/status/2117393668097310944"}, {"author_id": "1543134949808558080", "conversation_id": "2117375878900621755", "created_at": "2026-11-02T23:06:25.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117392918499717374"], "id": "2117392918499717374", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 47, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus It found an error in the weights that qwen already addressed was present. It’s cool but it’s not a giant step at all lol", "url": "https://x.com/JngPing/status/2117392918499717374"}, {"author_id": "1751912427938000896", "conversation_id": "2117375878900621755", "created_at": "2026-11-02T23:00:53.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117391523134218555"], "id": "2117391523134218555", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 20, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus The fact that astra found the loop is just amazing by itself", "url": "https://x.com/lddrums20/status/2117391523134218555"}, {"author_id": "1657085783507886094", "conversation_id": "2117375878900621755", "created_at": "2026-11-02T22:50:21.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117388873932406886"], "id": "2117388873932406886", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus Models writing working weights directly instead of training them is wild if it holds up. Curious how it does once people try to replicate it.", "url": "https://x.com/rufo_ai/status/2117388873932406886"}, {"author_id": "2308409648", "conversation_id": "2117375878900621755", "created_at": "2026-11-02T22:45:58.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117387773292462535"], "id": "2117387773292462535", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 20, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus Good thing we have so much open sourced weights!\n\nGuys are going to go wild on them.", "url": "https://x.com/cryptomessenger/status/2117387773292462535"}, {"author_id": "500779282", "conversation_id": "2117375878900621755", "created_at": "2026-11-02T22:44:31.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117387408350347456"], "id": "2117387408350347456", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus Following the GPT-6 Astra weight-editing study, researchers report Claude models can write entire, functional neural net weights from scratch, a big step toward recursive self-improvement. https://t.co/GoiDyKxxfh", "url": "https://x.com/what_going_on_X/status/2117387408350347456"}, {"author_id": "1890047835728752640", "conversation_id": "2117375878900621755", "created_at": "2026-11-02T22:35:21.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117385098630951119"], "id": "2117385098630951119", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 45, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus worth reading Chandan's report to the end. all 10 algorithmic tasks hit 100% with hand-set weights, but the GCD \"program\" is a ~1M-unit MLP lookup table, not Euclid, and on SNLI the agent fit logistic regression on the eval set (the report calls that 100% invalid). great for", "url": "https://x.com/AiAdventurerx/status/2117385098630951119"}, {"author_id": "1473693715923406860", "conversation_id": "2117375878900621755", "created_at": "2026-11-02T22:31:20.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117384086822220156"], "id": "2117384086822220156", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 19, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus This is insane.", "url": "https://x.com/AGIapproaching/status/2117384086822220156"}, {"author_id": "1815021644315803648", "conversation_id": "2117375878900621755", "created_at": "2026-11-02T22:29:23.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117383597325750661"], "id": "2117383597325750661", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 77, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus This is likely exactly what Anthropic did with Opus 5.5 already", "url": "https://x.com/NotSpacewear/status/2117383597325750661"}, {"author_id": "2041941667607986176", "conversation_id": "2117375878900621755", "created_at": "2026-11-02T22:29:06.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117383526635213253"], "id": "2117383526635213253", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 10, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@LaireLaFlare @kimmonismus Just read it?", "url": "https://x.com/Fredlqbv/status/2117383526635213253"}, {"author_id": "894097934", "conversation_id": "2117375878900621755", "created_at": "2026-11-02T22:25:13.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117382550348091615"], "id": "2117382550348091615", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 118, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus did it write the weights by hand or write code that trains them", "url": "https://x.com/LaireLaFlare/status/2117382550348091615"}], "includes": {"users": [{"id": "1644034310993788928", "name": "froggernauter", "username": "froggernauter"}, {"id": "1358053503088918528", "name": "Bruce Wayne", "username": "RaelBrucewayne"}, {"id": "1720665183188922368", "name": "Grok", "username": "grok"}, {"id": "2102187446196719616", "name": "Markins", "username": "Markins7dku"}, {"id": "1331495798488653824", "name": "Nocky", "username": "NockyLucky"}, {"id": "102867203", "name": "Ruedana • AI • Building Seiri", "username": "RuedanaYT"}, {"id": "2110550226989711360", "name": "Plain AI Tips", "username": "plainAItips"}, {"id": "2116579414813065216", "name": "ContextWindowed", "username": "ContextWindowed"}, {"id": "2116797194372034560", "name": "Leo Chen", "username": "leochenlab"}, {"id": "2086370229396111360", "name": "AnAn❤️", "username": "miaojiang88"}, {"id": "2007976461031096320", "name": "DeepInTheNight", "username": "zhuhaotian512"}, {"id": "2094540909996048384", "name": "Ethan", "username": "EthanSDE"}, {"id": "417508671", "name": "The SI Maximalist", "username": "thesimaximalist"}, {"id": "2076808453176299520", "name": "MJ", "username": "MJmd26"}, {"id": "1543134949808558080", "name": "ping jng", "username": "JngPing"}, {"id": "1751912427938000896", "name": "Dan Swanson", "username": "lddrums20"}, {"id": "1657085783507886094", "name": "rufo.ai 💻", "username": "rufo_ai"}, {"id": "2308409648", "name": "Lando", "username": "cryptomessenger"}, {"id": "500779282", "name": "머선일이고?", "username": "what_going_on_X"}, {"id": "1890047835728752640", "name": "AI Adventurer", "username": "AiAdventurerx"}, {"id": "1473693715923406860", "name": "AI Pill ⏸️", "username": "AGIapproaching